+# Use `t` to validate PlaceBlock remote arguments
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [`t`](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker as a dependency, pinned to `=3.1.1` (the latest version on the Wally index).
+- Switches the `PlaceBlock` handler in `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau` from hand-written argument checks to a `t` validator. Remotes we add later can use the same approach.
+
+## How the dependency is added
+
+This repo manages packages with **pesde**, not a `wally.toml`. Wally packages come in through pesde's `[wally_indices]`. So `t` goes into `pesde.toml` the same way as Vide, Charm and the others:
+
+```toml
+t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }
+```
+
+After install, pesde writes the linker module `roblox_packages/t.luau`. Rojo already maps `roblox_packages` to `ReplicatedStorage.Packages`, so the handler loads it with `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)`. `default.project.json` doesn't need to change.
+
+## Behaviour of the PlaceBlock handler
+
+Every check the handler did before is still there:
+
+| Check | Before | After |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `blockTypeName` is a string | `typeof(...) ~= "string"` | `t.string` |
+| `position` is a `Vector3` | `typeof(...) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| `position` has no NaN components | `position ~= position` | custom `notNaN` check, combined with `t.Vector3` using `t.intersection` (`t.Vector3` does not reject NaN) |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName` lookup | unchanged |
+| Rate limit (`MIN_INTERVAL`) | | unchanged |
+| Character has a `HumanoidRootPart` | | unchanged |
+| Cell is not below Y=0 and not already filled | | unchanged |
+| Cell is within `MAX_REACH` | | unchanged |
+
+Invalid calls still return without doing anything, the same as before. Extra arguments are still ignored. The block-type lookup stays in the handler because it also returns the `BlockType` the handler uses.
+
+`t` checks don't narrow types for the Luau type checker, so the handler casts the arguments (`:: string`, `:: Vector3`) once the validator passes.
+
+## ⚠️ Before testing (reviewer action required)
+
+The packages were **not installed** while this change was written. That means `pesde.lock` has **not** been updated and `roblox_packages/t.luau` does not exist yet.
+
+1. Install dependencies with the pesde version pinned in `rokit.toml` (`pesde-pkg/pesde@0.7.4+registry.0.2.3`):
+   ```sh
+   rokit install   # only if your tools aren't up to date
+   pesde install
+   ```
+2. Check that `roblox_packages/t.luau` now exists. Without it, `BlockPlacement.server.luau` errors at startup on `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)`.
+3. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`** to this PR. It is tracked by git (`!pesde.lock` in `.gitignore`), and it should gain a `wally#osyrisrblx/t@3.1.1 roblox` entry.
+4. If you use luau-lsp, regenerate `sourcemap.json` (pesde's `sourcemap_generator` script or `rojo sourcemap`) so `t` resolves in the editor.
+
+## Test plan
+
+- [ ] `pesde install` succeeds and `pesde.lock` includes `t@3.1.1`
+- [ ] `rojo serve` / build, then play: the server starts with no script errors
+- [ ] Placing blocks with the normal client flow still works
+- [ ] Firing `PlaceBlock` from the command bar / an exploit-style client with bad arguments places nothing and throws no errors:
+  - [ ] non-string block name (e.g. `123`, `nil`)
+  - [ ] unknown block name (`"Lava"`)
+  - [ ] non-Vector3 position (e.g. `CFrame.new()`, `{}`)
+  - [ ] NaN position (`Vector3.new(0/0, 0, 0)`)
+- [ ] Rate limit, reach limit, occupied-cell and below-ground checks still reject as before
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
